# Cloudflare Pages headers for the Flutter web build.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 🔴 THE APP'S CONTENT-SECURITY-POLICY — ADDED 2026-09-09, [ADR 075].
#
# Until today this app shipped with NO CSP at all. `web/index.html` says so in
# its own comment ("MEASURED 2026-08-21 — apps/subscriptiontracker/web/_headers declares NO
# Content-Security-Policy at all … Do not read the absence of a CSP as
# permission"). That was survivable while the app owned a whole origin. It is
# not survivable now: the app is published at `nikatru.com/<id>`, which is the
# SAME ORIGIN as the marketing site, the pricing page, `/checkout-return` and
# the frozen consent archive — and the Supabase bearer token lives in that
# origin's web storage. An XSS here would reach all of it.
#
# 🔴 THIS FILE IS WHERE IT BELONGS, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF THE WHOLE ROUTING
# DESIGN. MEASURED 2026-09-09 on a throwaway Pages project: `_headers` is
# applied by the ASSET-serving stage, so `sites/nikatru/_headers` does NOT reach
# a response the apex router returns from a proxy fetch, while THIS file's rules
# travel with the app's bytes and do. A per-app policy is possible only because
# the router proxies rather than merging every app into one project — where a
# single `_headers` would have to hold the union, and the weakest policy would
# apply to everything.
#
# ── EVERY SOURCE BELOW WAS MEASURED, NOT GUESSED ─────────────────────────────
# Verified 2026-09-09 by serving THIS EXACT BUILD through a proxy carrying this
# exact policy and reading the browser console: the app booted to the onboarding
# screen with ZERO CSP violations. Each unobvious entry, and why it is there:
#
#   · `'wasm-unsafe-eval'` — CanvasKit/skwasm. NOT `'unsafe-eval'`: the narrow
#     keyword permits WebAssembly compilation and nothing else.
#   · `'sha256-SqMf+O735lfNTprKa7S7jIWl1q79qFSdJCsyK+SUFsM='` — the ONE inline
#     <script> in web/index.html, the boot loader. The hash was computed from the
#     repository's own bytes and CONFIRMED IDENTICAL to the value the browser
#     reported for the deployed page, which is the proof that `$FLUTTER_BASE_HREF`
#     substitution does not disturb it. assert-web-cache-policy.mjs recomputes it
#     on every run, so an edit to that script that forgets this line goes RED
#     instead of silently disabling the loader.
#   · ⏱ 2026-09-12 — `https://browser.sentry-cdn.com` IS GONE. sentry_flutter injected
#     the Sentry browser SDK from it; packages/telemetry now turns that off on web and
#     sends events with the Dart SDK's HTTP transport to glitchtip.nikatru.com
#     (`useHttpTransportOnWeb`, telemetry_bootstrap.dart). No third-party CDN is left.
#   · ⏱ 2026-09-12 — `https://www.gstatic.com` AND `https://fonts.gstatic.com` ARE
#     GONE, measured 2026-09-09 as CanvasKit and the Roboto/Noto font fallback.
#     The build now passes `--no-web-resources-cdn` (CanvasKit from `/canvaskit/*`)
#     and web/flutter_bootstrap.js passes `fontFallbackBaseUrl: "fallback-fonts/"`,
#     which deploy-web.yml fills with sha256-pinned copies
#     (tooling/web/self-host-fallback-fonts.mjs) and refuses to deploy without.
#   · `worker-src`/`child-src blob:` — the engine spawns its wasm workers from
#     blob URLs.
#   · `challenges.cloudflare.com` — Turnstile, in script-src AND frame-src. It is
#     declared BEFORE `vars.TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` is ever set, so the gate cannot
#     fail closed on the day it is switched on. ⚠️ The widget's own configured
#     domain list is a SEPARATE console setting and still names the old subdomain.
#   · `connect-src` names the four first-party hosts the app calls. It does NOT
#     name the apex, because `'self'` IS the apex once the app is served there.
#
# ⚠️ `frame-ancestors 'none'` and `X-Frame-Options: DENY` are both set: the app
# must not be framed, including by another path on its own origin, because
# same-origin framing is otherwise unrestricted between app paths on one apex.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'sha256-SqMf+O735lfNTprKa7S7jIWl1q79qFSdJCsyK+SUFsM=' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; child-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' https://lcrkiurkvzhkonjwhpiv.supabase.co https://subscriptiontracker-api.nikatru.com https://config.nikatru.com https://platform.nikatru.com https://glitchtip.nikatru.com; upgrade-insecure-requests
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 🔴 WHY THIS FILE EXISTS — [pipeline 9]R-9, the cache limb.
#
# deploy-web.yml builds with `--pwa-strategy=none` ([ADR 023], LOCKED
# 2026-07-31: the service worker was rejected deliberately, it is not an
# oversight). So there is NO service worker and no client-side update
# machinery on the ONLY channel this factory serves. That leaves the HTTP
# cache as the entire update mechanism, and until this file existed nothing in
# the repository CHOSE a policy for it — `flutter build web` emits no
# `_headers` and the deploy ships `build/web` straight to Pages, so whatever
# the platform defaults to was what a returning visitor got.
#
# The failure that produces is not a slow update. It is a client running the
# PREVIOUS build with no way to know: the force-update gate (CFG-1) compares
# the version the app REPORTS, and a stale `flutter_bootstrap.js` reports the
# old one honestly. The kill-switch cannot see a client the cache is hiding
# from it.
#
# Flutter copies `web/` verbatim into `build/web`, so this file is deployed as
# a sibling of index.html and Pages reads it from the deployed directory.
#
# ⚠️ THE SPLIT IS BY WHETHER THE NAME CARRIES A HASH, not by file type. A
# STABLE name with CHANGING content must be revalidated every build; a name
# that changes when its bytes change can be cached forever, because a new
# build simply asks for a different name.
#
# `must-revalidate` with `max-age=0` is a conditional request, not a full
# download: the browser asks, the edge answers 304 when nothing moved. The
# cost of correctness here is one round trip.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 🔴 2026-08-04 — THE RULE ABOVE WAS RIGHT AND THIS FILE WAS APPLYING IT TO THE
#    WRONG SET. `/assets/*`, `/canvaskit/*` and `/icons/*` were declared
#    `immutable, max-age=31536000` under the comment "content-addressed output:
#    the name changes when the bytes do". THAT IS NOT TRUE OF THIS BUNDLE, and
#    it was never verified — it was inherited from how a webpack-style build
#    behaves.
#
# MEASURED against the live channel (the app's former subdomain), not reasoned:
#
#   · `flutter_bootstrap.js` names its dependencies `main.dart.js`,
#     `canvaskit.js` and `canvaskit.wasm` — plain, unhashed. A scan of the
#     whole bootstrap for a hash-shaped token returned NONE.
#   · The only `?v=` in the bootstrap is on `flutter_service_worker.js`, a file
#     `--pwa-strategy=none` never emits. So no asset request carries a
#     cache-busting query either.
#   · The real files under `/assets/` are `AssetManifest.bin.json`,
#     `FontManifest.json`, `NOTICES` and `fonts/MaterialIcons-Regular.otf` —
#     fixed names whose CONTENT changes whenever the app's asset list does.
#   · `/icons/Icon-192.png` and friends are copied verbatim from `web/icons/`
#     in this repository. PR #149 changed exactly those bytes.
#
# NOTHING IN THIS BUNDLE IS CONTENT-ADDRESSED. So `immutable` — which tells a
# browser not to revalidate even on an explicit reload — meant a returning
# visitor kept the previous launcher icon, font and asset manifest for up to a
# YEAR. The same failure this file was written to prevent, one directory down,
# behind a green guard: `assert-web-cache-policy.mjs` only ever asked about the
# three entry points, and its own test suite asserted that "hashed output under
# assets/ staying immutable does NOT fire".
#
# The guard now derives the question from the tree instead: every file this
# repository ships under `web/` keeps its name through `flutter build web`, so
# the rule governing its URL must revalidate. `/favicon.png` below is there for
# the same reason — it was undeclared and correct only by inheriting the
# platform default, which is the state this whole file exists to end.
#
# ⚠️ IF A FUTURE FLUTTER EMITS CONTENT-HASHED NAMES, THIS FLIPS BACK — for those
# names only, and the evidence for the flip is a fresh look at what
# `flutter_bootstrap.js` actually asks for, not this comment.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️ ONE RULE PER PATH, DELIBERATELY. Cloudflare Pages documents that "an
# incoming request which matches multiple rules' URL patterns will inherit all
# rules' headers", and that a header set twice is JOINED WITH A COMMA. Two
# rules that both match one path therefore produce
# `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000,
# immutable` — a single self-contradicting header, not an override. The rules
# below are written as disjoint classes so that never arises.

# The stable-named entry points. A new deploy MUST be visible immediately.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/flutter_bootstrap.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/version.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# main.dart.js is emitted under a STABLE name by `flutter build web`, so it is
# an entry point by the rule above even though it is compiled output.
/main.dart.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Shipped verbatim from web/ and named in index.html. Stable name, changing
# content — the launcher icon and favicon are the exact bytes PR #149 replaced.
/favicon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/icons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Build output under a FIXED name: the asset and font manifests, NOTICES, the
# bundled fonts, and the CanvasKit engine (whose bytes track the Flutter SDK).
# None of these carry a hash, so none of them may be immutable.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/canvaskit/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# The engine's text fallback fonts, copied into build/web/fallback-fonts/ by
# tooling/web/self-host-fallback-fonts.mjs (see apps/<id>/web/flutter_bootstrap.js).
# Not shipped from web/, and the SAME rule as the bundle's other build output:
# a fixed name per engine version, so revalidate rather than assume immutability.
/fallback-fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
